;;; The control of `symmetric-derived-root.ein` — **W98**, register row
;;; `W98/derived-at-root`'s control (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`).
;;;
;;; The same program with the mark written as a fact, `(__symmetric__ near)`,
;;; and not derived by a rule. Nothing else differs. Root's fixpoint holds
;;; `(near a b)` and `(near b a)`, the second by the native mirror; the blind
;;; enumerator has nothing to propose, and R is {∅}, which is the witness's
;;; right answer. One symmetry stated two ways is one symmetry.

(relation near Thing Thing :why "{?1} is near {?2}")
(near a b)
(__symmetric__ near)
(query :goal (near ?x ?y))
